  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThe current WebKit implementation behaves as below:\n\n```js\nconst input = document.createElement(\"input\");\ninput.type = \"color\";\ninput.value = \"red\";\ninput.value // gives `#ff0000`\ninput.colorSpace = \"display-p3\";\ninput.value // gives `color(display-p3 ...)`\ninput.colorSpace = \"limited-srgb\";\ninput.value // back to `#ff0000`\n```\n\nBut colorSpace setter per the spec doesn't trigger [value sanitization algorithm](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/input.html#value-sanitization-algorithm). It seems WebKit runs [the sanitization on getter](https://searchfox.org/wubkat/rev/021be8e5aefd8742e091c6369be13fd745207359/Source/WebCore/html/HTMLInputElement.cpp#1147) and thus this just works, but probably needs some spec addition to make it happen per-spec.\n\ncc @annevk ",
